<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 15 October, from 1582 to 1917.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1582 CE <span class="tih-ago">444 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Gregorian calendar takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Friday 15 October 1582 was the first day of the Gregorian calendar in Italy, Spain, Portugal and Poland, following directly on Thursday 4 October. Protestant and Orthodox countries adopted it only over the following centuries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1783 CE <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pilâtre de Rozier makes the first human balloon ascent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Paris, Jean-François Pilâtre de Rozier rose about 25 metres in a tethered Montgolfier hot-air balloon, the first human ascent. Five weeks later he made the first free flight.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1815 CE <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon arrives in exile at Saint Helena</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">HMS Northumberland anchored off Jamestown, Saint Helena, carrying the defeated Napoleon. On this remote South Atlantic island he spent his last six years, dying there in 1821.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1880 CE <span class="tih-ago">146 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cologne Cathedral is completed after 632 years</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Kaiser Wilhelm I attended celebrations marking the completion of Cologne Cathedral. Begun in 1248 and left unfinished for centuries, the Gothic church was completed using its medieval plans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">Wilhelm I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mata Hari is executed by a French firing squad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dutch-born dancer Margaretha Zelle, known as Mata Hari, was shot at Vincennes after conviction as a German spy. Historians still dispute how much, if any, useful intelligence she passed on.</p></div></li></ol>
